ke lint and make typecheck clean; gen_types --check up to date. make verify running now; push to Gerrit follows a clean verify.","timestamp":1794360927310708297},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"2026-11-10 18:55 PST: make verify exit 0 on 4d9a5147f39 (20910 + 202 integration passed; 18:05-18:53 PST). An earlier run inside the agent sandbox failed 45+6 tests on blocked sockets/git (environment, not code; those 14 files pass 296/296 unsandboxed). Pushed as Gerrit change 3342; awaiting LLM-Review and Verified.","timestamp":1794365664591594794},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-10 ~19:00 PST (session 3d705fec): in_progress, claimed. Commit 4d9a5147f391c30d110827d29d0d46d00ba3e936 in .rebar/worktrees/fixver-epic implements Approach 1-9; make verify exit 0 (log .rebar/scratch/3d705fec/make-verify-c2b.log in that worktree). Gerrit change 3342 pushed, no LLM-Review/Verified votes yet, 0 unresolved. Next: wait for LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 (address findings with amend --no-edit + re-push), then scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py 3342 --revision <current full SHA>, fast-forward the worktree to origin/main, tick AC boxes, close. Note: run make verify outside the agent sandbox; inside it 51 socket/git tests fail for environment reasons.","timestamp":1794365693396849440}],"created_at":1794256384786047001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"146a0953-d1df-463a-86e0-f251f617a4c7","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"0f4c-4586-8f3e-432d"},{"link_uuid":"96e774b5-9833-4831-9a65-466943bf14df","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c2ab-1ecc-7f39-4d37"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nEpic `inferior-seaborgium-aruanas` needs a `releases` field in compiled state before any sync or surface can use it; today there is none (`src/rebar/reducer/_state.py:28-89`). ADR 0124 fixes the design: Jira version names carried by a new `RELEASE_DELTA` event with `TAG_DELTA`'s fold rules, and `SCHEMA_VERSION` 6.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. **Event type.** In `src/rebar/reducer/_version.py`, add a single-source constant `RELEASE_DELTA = \"RELEASE_DELTA\"` beside `TAG_DELTA` (line 77), add it to `KNOWN_EVENT_TYPES` (lines 88-123), and bump `SCHEMA_VERSION` from 5 to 6 (line 41), with a comment naming ADR 0124.\n2. **Fold.** In `src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py`, add `process_release_delta(state, data)` next to `process_tag_delta` (lines 429-449). Same rules on `state[\"releases\"]`: non-list bodies act as empty, non-string or empty names are skipped, removals first, then additions, idempotent. Extract `process_tag_delta`'s body into `_fold_list_delta(state, key, data)` and call it from both; `test_reducer_tag_delta.py` guards the extraction.\n3. **Dispatch.** Register `RELEASE_DELTA: lambda c: process_release_delta(c.state, c.data)` in the replay dispatch table in `src/rebar/reducer/_replay.py` (beside line 109).\n4. **Default.** Add `\"releases\": []` to `make_initial_state` (`src/rebar/reducer/_state.py`), right after `\"tags\"`.\n5. **Write path.** Add `RELEASE_DELTA` to `EVENT_TYPES` in `src/rebar/_store/event_prepare.py` (the allow-list at lines 33-60) and to the allowed-types message (line 125), so the store accepts the event. Add `\"RELEASE_DELTA\"` to `_AUTO_RECOVER_ORPHAN_TYPES` in `src/rebar/_commands/fsck_repair.py:37-39`, beside `TAG_DELTA`.\n6. **Reducer cache.** Bump `_REDUCER_CACHE_VERSION` in `src/rebar/reducer/_cache.py:31` from 8 to 9 (`# 9: releases field + RELEASE_DELTA fold (ADR 0124)`). The cache key is that version plus event file stats (`_cache.py:128`), and lines 29-30 require an increment when projection semantics change; otherwise old-binary caches come back without `releases`.\n7. **Snapshot.** No change: compaction stores the reduced state (`src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:688-705`) and `process_snapshot` restores every key (`_processors.py:464-468`); a pre-feature snapshot keeps the `[]` default.\n8. **Schema.** Add an optional `releases` property (array of strings, description naming ADR 0124) to `src/rebar/schemas/ticket_state.schema.json`, not `required`. Regenerate `src/rebar/types.py` with `python -m rebar.schemas.gen_types`.\n9. **Docs.** In `docs/event-schema.md`, add a `RELEASE_DELTA` row to the replayed-event table (beside the `TAG_DELTA` row at line 46), and record v6 in the \"Schema version & forward compatibility\" history: a new event body type, so older clones preserve and ignore it, and the reconcile host is upgraded first.\n\nNo writer of `RELEASE_DELTA` exists after this change except tests; the inbound, outbound and surface children add writers.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/reducer/_version.py` (constant, known types, schema version)\n- `src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py` (shared list-delta fold, `process_release_delta`)\n- `src/rebar/reducer/_replay.py` (dispatch)\n- `src/rebar/reducer/_state.py` (default)\n- `src/rebar/reducer/_cache.py` (cache version 9)\n- `src/rebar/_store/event_prepare.py` (write allow-list)\n- `src/rebar/_commands/fsck_repair.py` (append-only type set)\n- `src/rebar/schemas/ticket_state.schema.json`, `src/rebar/types.py` (generated)\n- `docs/event-schema.md`\n- `tests/scripts/reducer/test_reducer_release_delta.py` (new)\n- `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_event_schema_forward_compat.py` (extend)\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_release_delta_store.py` (new: store append, compaction, stale cache)\n\n## Testing\n\nNew `tests/scripts/reducer/test_reducer_release_delta.py`, in the style of `test_reducer_tag_delta.py`:\n- happy path: `{\"added\": [\"2.4\"]}` then `{\"added\": [\"2.5\"], \"removed\": [\"2.4\"]}` reduces to `[\"2.5\"]`;\n- add beats remove in one event: `{\"added\": [\"2.4\"], \"removed\": [\"2.4\"]}` yields `[\"2.4\"]`;\n- idempotent: the same `{\"added\": [\"2.4\"]}` delta written twice (two events) yields `[\"2.4\"]`, and a remove of an absent name changes nothing;\n- two concurrent adds from different clones both survive;\n- malformed bodies (`added: \"2.4\"`, `added: [1, \"\"]`) leave `[]` without raising;\n- no `RELEASE_DELTA` events yields `releases == []`, and a `RELEASE_DELTA` leaves `tags` unchanged;\n- a pre-feature `SNAPSHOT` (no `releases` key) followed by a `RELEASE_DELTA` yields the delta's names;\n- a reducer with `RELEASE_DELTA` masked out of `KNOWN_EVENT_TYPES` ignores it without error (as `test_downgraded_clone_preserves_and_ignores` does for tags).\n\nNew `tests/interfaces/store/test_release_delta_store.py`, in the style of `tests/interfaces/store/test_workflow_run_state.py`:\n- `_seam.append_event(tid, \"RELEASE_DELTA\", {...})` succeeds through the store write path and `rebar.show_ticket` returns the names;\n- `rebar store compact <tid> --threshold=0` writes a `SNAPSHOT` whose `compiled_state.releases` holds the names, and a later `show_ticket` returns the same list;\n- stale cache: forge a `.cache.json` keyed with `_REDUCER_CACHE_VERSION = 8` holding a state without `releases` for a ticket that has a `RELEASE_DELTA` (as `tests/unit/test_reducer_status.py:129-150` does for version 7), then `reduce_ticket` returns the delta's names.\n\nExtend `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_event_schema_forward_compat.py`: `RELEASE_DELTA` is in `KNOWN_EVENT_TYPES` and `SCHEMA_VERSION == 6`. Existing guards: that file's `test_known_event_types_equals_the_reducer_dispatch_table` pins dispatch, and `tests/interfaces/store/test_fsck_snapshot_checks.py:122` (fsck sets cover every known type but CREATE/SNAPSHOT) pins the fsck edit.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `make_initial_state()[\"releases\"] == []`; pinned by the no-event reducer test.\n- [ ] A `RELEASE_DELTA` applies removals before additions, with an add winning when one name is in both lists; pinned by the happy-path and add-wins tests.\n- [ ] Repeating a `RELEASE_DELTA` changes nothing; pinned by the idempotency test.\n- [ ] A `RELEASE_DELTA` never changes `tags`; pinned by the no-leak test.\n- [ ] `SNAPSHOT` compaction preserves `releases`; pinned by the store compaction test.\n- [ ] A pre-feature snapshot replays to `[]` and then accepts later deltas; pinned by the pre-feature snapshot test.\n- [ ] The store accepts a `RELEASE_DELTA` append; pinned by the store append test.\n- [ ] A reducer cache written under version 8 is recomputed, so `releases` appears; pinned by the stale-cache test.\n- [ ] `RELEASE_DELTA` is in `KNOWN_EVENT_TYPES` and `SCHEMA_VERSION == 6`; pinned by the forward-compat contract test.\n- [ ] `RELEASE_DELTA` is in fsck's auto-recover orphan set; pinned by `tests/interfaces/store/test_fsck_snapshot_checks.py`.\n- [ ] A reducer without `RELEASE_DELTA` in its known types ignores the event; pinned by the masked-reducer test.\n- [ ] `tests/scripts/reducer/test_reducer_tag_delta.py` passes unchanged.\n- [ ] `python -m rebar.schemas.gen_types --check` exits 0.\n- [ ] `docs/event-schema.md` has a `RELEASE_DELTA` row and a v6 history entry.\n- [ ] `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify` exits 0 on the commit pushed for review.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/reducer/_version.py","reason":"RELEASE_DELTA type, schema v6"},{"path":"src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py","reason":"list-delta fold"},{"path":"src/rebar/reducer/_replay.py","reason":"dispatch"},{"path":"src/rebar/reducer/_state.py","reason":"releases default"},{"path":"src/rebar/reducer/_cache.py","reason":"cache version 9"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/event_prepare.py","reason":"write allow-list"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/fsck_repair.py","reason":"auto-recover orphan set"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/ticket_state.schema.json","reason":"releases property"},{"path":"src/rebar/types.py","reason":"regenerated types"},{"path":"docs/event-schema.md","reason":"event row and v6 history"},{"path":"tests/scripts/reducer/test_reducer_release_delta.py","reason":"new reducer tests"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_release_delta_store.py","reason":"store append, compaction, stale cache"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_event_schema_forward_compat.py","reason":"known type and version"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["depends_on","0f4c-4586-8f3e-432d"],["parent","21ec-3e9b-4a27-4775"],["relates_to","c2ab-1ecc-7f39-4d37"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"21ec-3e9b-4a27-4775","parent_status_uuid":"962b429f-2cab-4a0a-a1ef-ed89a40df106","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3a2b-a8db-d642-44ab","ticket_type":"story","title":"Store releases in compiled ticket state via a RELEASE_DELTA event","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2cb8a182-6fb9-4917-b536-63821878fe67","9f9abcd5-ebb2-4892-8d46-80d9c9c29044","435957d6-48be-4a10-aac9-f1cc872a5f58","af8d4693-e55f-4d39-8e8c-279c04f213fa","c23aa982-e8eb-40eb-9dd2-6cbe298ff674","cb6386d7-266b-4085-a2de-77fbfeac3a1c","962b429f-2cab-4a0a-a1ef-ed89a40df106","07d19515-db30-4947-baf1-705c79820c07","1a24859f-7646-4fae-ba84-79e035d3818e","44efea8a-263c-479c-ad06-4014ad924da5","971149b5-5f43-41bc-b676-bf8662dc133c","96e774b5-9833-4831-9a65-466943bf14df"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794366031146449582,"uuid":"88c561c2-dee5-4c9e-b8ab-6b6dd57dbeb6"}